, editor or charts\n    small: one interactive widget, read-only; typical: one interactive widget with 2-3 actions; large: two widgets, or real-time updates; very-large: several linked widgets with real-time collaboration\n- ui-shell (web, mobile): The app shell: navigation, layout, theme, sign-in wiring, error pages\n    small: one layout, up to 4 menu items; typical: one layout, roles in the menu, light theme; large: several layouts, two languages or both colour modes; very-large: several apps or right-to-left plus the above\n- ui-device (web, mobile): A client-side capability: push, camera, payment sheet, deep links, offline\n    small: one capability, default UI; typical: one capability with permissions and errors; large: two capabilities, or offline sync of one entity; very-large: offline-first across several entities\n- qa-cases (qa): Test plan and cases for a feature\n    small: one flow, happy path and errors; typical: 2-4 flows; large: 5-8 flows or several roles; very-large: over 8 flows\n- qa-e2e (qa): Automated end-to-end tests for a flow\n    small: one short flow; typical: one flow with its error paths; large: 2-3 flows or several platforms; very-large: a full regression suite\n- qa-uat (qa): Client acceptance testing or a regression pass\n    small: half a day; typical: one round; large: two rounds; very-large: three or more rounds\n- design-screen (design): Designing a screen\n    small: a variant of an existing screen; typical: a new screen with its states; large: a complex screen; very-large: a complex screen on several platforms\n- design-system (design): Design system: tokens, components, guidelines\n    small: tokens only; typical: tokens and core components; large: full component set; very-large: full set on several platforms\n- gd-assets (gd): Graphic assets: icons, illustrations, brand pieces\n    small: up to 5 assets; typical: 6-15 assets; large: 16-30 assets; very-large: over 30 assets\n- ops-setup (backend, web, mobile): Environments, CI/C